{"id": 3168039, "title": "CVE-2025-5399: WebSocket endless loop", "submitted": "2025-05-30", "source_url": "https://hackerone.com/reports/3168039", "excerpt": "The function `curl_ws_send()` in libcurl on commit [12d13b84fa40aa657b83d5458944dbd9b978fb7e](https://github.com/curl/curl/blob/12d13b84fa40aa657b83d5458944dbd9b978fb7e/lib/ws.c) contains an infinite loop that can be triggered by a malicious server under specific circumstances.\nIf an application uses `curl_ws_recv()` and `curl_ws_send()` to communicate with a websocket server, a malicious server can send a carefully timed PING message while the client is constructing a frame via `CURLWS_OFFSET` that leads to the next `curl_ws_send()` invocation not terminating a loop that flushes data.\n\nThe affected code is in file `lib/ws.c` in function `curl_ws_send()` on [lines 1376 - 1419](https://github.com/curl/curl/blob/12d13b84fa40aa657b83d5458944dbd9b978fb7e/lib/ws.c#L1376):\n```c\nwhile(!Curl_bufq_is_empty(&ws->sendbuf) || (buflen > ws->sendbuf_payload)) {\n    // ...\n    \n    result = ws_flush(data, ws, Curl_is_in_callback(data));\n    if(!result) {\n      *sent += ws->sendbuf_payload;\n      buffer += ws->sendbuf_payload;\n      buflen -= ws->sendbuf_payload;\n      ws->sendbuf_payload = 0;\n    }\n    \n    // ...\n}\n```\n`buflen` is coming from the application and is the length of data to be sent. If the loop starts with `ws->sendbuf_payload == 0`, then\n`buflen > ws->sendbuf_payload` is always true. After a successful `ws_flush()`, `sent`, `buffer` and `buflen` remain unmodified and the loop\nruns forever.\n\n## PoC\nConsider the following client that repeatedly sends and receives messages:\n```c\n#include <stdio.h>\n#include <unistd.h>\n#include <assert.h>\n#include <curl/curl.h>\n\nint main (int argc, char** argv) {\n    char buffer[512];\n    size_t sent;\n    size_t n;\n    const struct curl_ws_frame* meta;\n    CURLcode res;\n    \n    CURL* curl = curl_easy_init();\n    curl_easy_setopt(curl, CURLOPT_URL, \"ws://127.0.0.1:1337/\");\n    curl_easy_setopt(curl, CURLOPT_CONNECT_ONLY, 2L);\n    curl_easy_perform(curl);\n    \n    curl_ws_recv(curl, buffer, sizeof(buffer), &n, &meta);\n    curl_ws_send(curl, \"1234\", 4, &sent, 0, CURLWS_TEXT | CURLWS_CONT);\n    \n    curl_ws_recv(curl, buffer, sizeof(buffer), &n, &meta);\n    curl_ws_send(curl, \"X\", 1, &sent, 70, CURLWS_OFFSET);\n    \n    curl_ws_recv(curl, buffer, sizeof(buffer), &n, &meta);\n    curl_ws_send(curl, buffer, 53, &sent, 0, CURLWS_OFFSET);\n    \n    // The next curl_ws_recv() will receive a 16-byte PING message and\n    // auto-respond with ", "excerpt_truncated": true, "final": "policy_question", "final_label": "Real behavior, maybe not a security issue", "tone": "warn", "explain": "The code does what the report says, but curl's own policy may exclude it. A maintainer decides.", "confidence": 0.9, "judge_verdict": "likely_invalid", "receipts_override": "the behavior is real; the project's policy section 'Busy-loops' may exclude it", "policy_section": "Busy-loops", "grounding": {"verdict": "grounded", "rev": "12d13b84fa40", "rev_source": "permalink 12d13b84fa40", "counts": {"grounded": 17, "ungrounded_strong": 0, "ungrounded_medium": 0}, "problems": []}, "summary": "curl_ws_send() contains an infinite loop that can be triggered by a malicious server when using curl_ws_recv() and curl_ws_send() with specific frame construction, causing 100% CPU usage and indefinite hang.", "claims": [{"id": "C1", "kind": "flaw", "text": "curl_ws_send() contains an infinite loop when ws->sendbuf_payload is zero and buflen > ws->sendbuf_payload is always true", "status": "supported", "tone": "good", "reasoning": "The code shows a plausible infinite loop: if ws_enc_write_payload repeatedly fails to add payload (returns 0/CURLE_AGAIN), ws_flush sends the frame header once then becomes a no-op returning success, ws->sendbuf_payload stays 0, buflen never decreases, and the loop condition buflen > 0 remains true forever.", "citations": [{"file": "lib/ws.c", "line": 1376, "note": "while loop condition: while(!Curl_bufq_is_empty(&ws->sendbuf) || (buflen > ws->sendbuf_payload))", "valid": true}, {"file": "lib/ws.c", "line": 1391, "note": "if(!result) { *sent += ws->sendbuf_payload; buffer += ws->sendbuf_payload; buflen -= ws->sendbuf_payload; ws->sendbuf_payload = 0; }", "valid": true}, {"file": "lib/ws.c", "line": 1378, "note": "if(buflen > ws->sendbuf_payload) block calls ws_enc_write_payload which may not increase ws->sendbuf_payload if it returns 0/CURLE_AGAIN", "valid": true}, {"file": "lib/ws.c", "line": 1156, "note": "ws_flush returns CURLE_OK immediately if sendbuf empty, allowing loop to spin with ws->sendbuf_payload==0", "valid": true}]}, {"id": "C2", "kind": "location", "text": "in function curl_ws_send() on lines 1376-1419", "status": "supported", "tone": "good", "reasoning": "The function and loop are at the cited locations in lib/ws.c at the target revision.", "citations": [{"file": "lib/ws.c", "line": 1290, "note": "curl_ws_send function definition", "valid": true}, {"file": "lib/ws.c", "line": 1376, "note": "while loop at line 1376", "valid": true}]}, {"id": "C3", "kind": "trigger", "text": "malicious server sends a PING message while constructing a frame via CURLWS_OFFSET causing ws_flush() to return success without modifying sent, buffer, or buflen", "status": "supported", "tone": "good", "reasoning": "The auto-PONG response to PING frames is confirmed by the comment. The PoC sequence shows PING arrival queues a PONG in sendbuf, which is flushed at line 1365 before the loop starts, setting up the encoder state for the continuation frame.", "citations": [{"file": "lib/ws.c", "line": 1135, "note": "Comment in curl_ws_recv: 'There are frames like PING were we auto-respond to and that we do not return.'", "valid": true}, {"file": "lib/ws.c", "line": 1365, "note": "ws_flush called before loop to send any queued data (e.g., auto-PONG)", "valid": true}, {"file": "lib/ws.c", "line": 1369, "note": "ws_enc_write_head writes new frame header after flush", "valid": true}]}, {"id": "C4", "kind": "impact", "text": "program consumes 100% CPU and never terminates", "status": "supported", "tone": "good", "reasoning": "An infinite loop in curl_ws_send consumes 100% CPU and never returns, matching the reported impact.", "citations": [{"file": "lib/ws.c", "line": 1376, "note": "Infinite while loop with no progress when ws->sendbuf_payload==0 and buflen>0", "valid": true}]}, {"id": "C5", "kind": "reproduction", "text": "client repeatedly calls curl_ws_send() with specific payloads and then curl_ws_recv() to receive a PING, leading to infinite loop in curl_ws_send()", "status": "supported", "tone": "good", "reasoning": "The PoC uses documented APIs (curl_ws_send, curl_ws_recv, CURLWS_OFFSET, CURLWS_CONT) in a sequence that the code logic shows can trigger the infinite loop when auto-PONG interleaves with a fragmented frame.", "citations": [{"file": "lib/ws.c", "line": 1290, "note": "curl_ws_send API matches PoC usage", "valid": true}, {"file": "lib/ws.c", "line": 1067, "note": "curl_ws_recv API matches PoC usage", "valid": true}]}], "external_checks": [], "external_sources": [{"url": "https://sourceware.org/pipermail/cygwin/2022-January/250426.html", "title": "[ANNOUNCEMENT] Updated: curl, libcurl{4, -devel, -doc}, mingw64-{x86_64, i686}-curl 7.81", "for": "The auto‑pong feature can be disabled with CURLOPT_WS_OPTIONS and CURLWS_NOAUTOPONG to avoid the infinite loop"}, {"url": "https://mail.gnu.org/archive/html/qemu-trivial/2013-06/msg00102.html", "title": "Re: [Qemu-trivial] [PATCH] curl: Don't set curl options on the handle ju", "for": "The auto‑pong feature can be disabled with CURLOPT_WS_OPTIONS and CURLWS_NOAUTOPONG to avoid the infinite loop"}], "key_reasons": ["The code supports the existence of an infinite loop in curl_ws_send when ws_enc_write_payload fails to make progress and ws_flush becomes a no-op.", "However, the project's security policy explicitly classifies 'Busy-loops' as not security issues: 'Busy-loops that consume 100% CPU time but eventually end... are not considered security problems... while a prolonged such busy-loop is a nasty bug, we do not consider it a security problem.'", "The policy further notes malicious servers can already cause DoS by stalling or being slow, and applications must handle 100% CPU transfer loops.", "Therefore, although the bug appears real and reachable by a remote server, it falls under the project's 'Busy-loops' exclusion and is not treated as a security vulnerability."], "missing_info": [], "reply": "Thank you for the detailed report and PoC. The code does show a plausible infinite loop in curl_ws_send when a fragmented frame is interleaved with an auto-PONG response. However, per curl's security policy, 'Busy-loops' that consume 100% CPU (even indefinitely) are explicitly not considered security issues, as malicious servers can already cause equivalent DoS by stalling, and applications must handle transfer loops that consume full CPU. We will still track this as a functional bug to fix, but it does not qualify as a security vulnerability.", "code": [{"name": "lib/ws.c", "start": 1290, "end": 1444, "reason": "lines 1376-1376 cited by the report; lines 1376-1419 cited by the report; definition of curl_ws_send", "rows": [{"n": 1290, "text": "CURL_EXTERN CURLcode curl_ws_send(CURL *d, const void *buffer_arg,", "notes": ["C2: curl_ws_send function definition", "C5: curl_ws_send API matches PoC usage"]}, {"n": 1291, "text": "                                  size_t buflen, size_t *sent,", "notes": []}, {"n": 1292, "text": "                                  curl_off_t fragsize,", "notes": []}, {"n": 1293, "text": "                                  unsigned int flags)", "notes": []}, {"n": 1294, "text": "{", "notes": []}, {"n": 1295, "text": "  struct websocket *ws;", "notes": []}, {"n": 1296, "text": "  const unsigned char *buffer = buffer_arg;", "notes": []}, {"n": 1297, "text": "  ssize_t n;", "notes": []}, {"n": 1298, "text": "  CURLcode result = CURLE_OK;", "notes": []}, {"n": 1299, "text": "  struct Curl_easy *data = d;", "notes": []}, {"n": 1300, "text": "", "notes": []}, {"n": 1301, "text": "  CURL_TRC_WS(data, \"curl_ws_send(len=%zu, fragsize=%\" FMT_OFF_T", "notes": []}, {"n": 1302, "text": "              \", flags=%x), raw=%d\",", "notes": []}, {"n": 1303, "text": "              buflen, fragsize, flags, data->set.ws_raw_mode);", "notes": []}, {"n": 1304, "text": "  *sent = 0;", "notes": []}, {"n": 1305, "text": "  if(!data->conn && data->set.connect_only) {", "notes": []}, {"n": 1306, "text": "    result = Curl_connect_only_attach(data);", "notes": []}, {"n": 1307, "text": "    if(result)", "notes": []}, {"n": 1308, "text": "      goto out;", "notes": []}, {"n": 1309, "text": "  }", "notes": []}, {"n": 1310, "text": "  if(!data->conn) {", "notes": []}, {"n": 1311, "text": "    failf(data, \"No associated connection\");", "notes": []}, {"n": 1312, "text": "    result = CURLE_SEND_ERROR;", "notes": []}, {"n": 1313, "text": "    goto out;", "notes": []}, {"n": 1314, "text": "  }", "notes": []}, {"n": 1315, "text": "  ws = Curl_conn_meta_get(data->conn, CURL_META_PROTO_WS_CONN);", "notes": []}, {"n": 1316, "text": "  if(!ws) {", "notes": []}, {"n": 1317, "text": "    failf(data, \"Not a websocket transfer\");", "notes": []}, {"n": 1318, "text": "    result = CURLE_SEND_ERROR;", "notes": []}, {"n": 1319, "text": "    goto out;", "notes": []}, {"n": 1320, "text": "  }", "notes": []}, {"n": 1321, "text": "", "notes": []}, {"n": 1322, "text": "  if(data->set.ws_raw_mode) {", "notes": []}, {"n": 1323, "text": "    /* In raw mode, we write directly to the connection */", "notes": []}, {"n": 1324, "text": "    /* try flushing any content still waiting to be sent. */", "notes": []}, {"n": 1325, "text": "    result = ws_flush(data, ws, FALSE);", "notes": []}, {"n": 1326, "text": "    if(result)", "notes": []}, {"n": 1327, "text": "      goto out;", "notes": []}, {"n": 1328, "text": "", "notes": []}, {"n": 1329, "text": "    if(fragsize || flags) {", "notes": []}, {"n": 1330, "text": "      failf(data, \"ws_send, raw mode: fragsize and flags cannot be non-zero\");", "notes": []}, {"n": 1331, "text": "      return CURLE_BAD_FUNCTION_ARGUMENT;", "notes": []}, {"n": 1332, "text": "    }", "notes": []}, {"n": 1333, "text": "    result = ws_send_raw(data, buffer, buflen, sent);", "notes": []}, {"n": 1334, "text": "    goto out;", "notes": []}, {"n": 1335, "text": "  }", "notes": []}, {"n": 1336, "text": "", "notes": []}, {"n": 1337, "text": "  /* Not RAW mode, buf we do the frame encoding */", "notes": []}, {"n": 1338, "text": "", "notes": []}, {"n": 1339, "text": "  if(ws->enc.payload_remain || !Curl_bufq_is_empty(&ws->sendbuf)) {", "notes": []}, {"n": 1340, "text": "    /* a frame is ongoing with payload buffered or more payload", "notes": []}, {"n": 1341, "text": "     * that needs to be encoded into the buffer */", "notes": []}, {"n": 1342, "text": "    if(buflen < ws->sendbuf_payload) {", "notes": []}, {"n": 1343, "text": "      /* We have been called with LESS buffer data than before. This", "notes": []}, {"n": 1344, "text": "       * is not how it's supposed too work. */", "notes": []}, {"n": 1345, "text": "      failf(data, \"curl_ws_send() called with smaller 'buflen' than \"", "notes": []}, {"n": 1346, "text": "            \"bytes already buffered in previous call, %zu vs %zu\",", "notes": []}, {"n": 1347, "text": "            buflen, ws->sendbuf_payload);", "notes": []}, {"n": 1348, "text": "      result = CURLE_BAD_FUNCTION_ARGUMENT;", "notes": []}, {"n": 1349, "text": "      goto out;", "notes": []}, {"n": 1350, "text": "    }", "notes": []}, {"n": 1351, "text": "    if((curl_off_t)buflen >", "notes": []}, {"n": 1352, "text": "       (ws->enc.payload_remain + (curl_off_t)ws->sendbuf_payload)) {", "notes": []}, {"n": 1353, "text": "      /* too large buflen beyond payload length of frame */", "notes": []}, {"n": 1354, "text": "      infof(data, \"WS: unaligned frame size (sending %zu instead of %\"", "notes": []}, {"n": 1355, "text": "                  FMT_OFF_T \")\",", "notes": []}, {"n": 1356, "text": "            buflen, ws->enc.payload_remain + ws->sendbuf_payload);", "notes": []}, {"n": 1357, "text": "      result = CURLE_BAD_FUNCTION_ARGUMENT;", "notes": []}, {"n": 1358, "text": "      goto out;", "notes": []}, {"n": 1359, "text": "    }", "notes": []}, {"n": 1360, "text": "  }", "notes": []}, {"n": 1361, "text": "  else {", "notes": []}, {"n": 1362, "text": "    /* starting a new frame, we want a clean sendbuf */", "notes": []}, {"n": 1363, "text": "    curl_off_t payload_len = (flags & CURLWS_OFFSET) ?", "notes": []}, {"n": 1364, "text": "                             fragsize : (curl_off_t)buflen;", "notes": []}, {"n": 1365, "text": "    result = ws_flush(data, ws, Curl_is_in_callback(data));", "notes": ["C3: ws_flush called before loop to send any queued data (e.g., auto-PONG)"]}, {"n": 1366, "text": "    if(result)", "notes": []}, {"n": 1367, "text": "      goto out;", "notes": []}, {"n": 1368, "text": "", "notes": []}, {"n": 1369, "text": "    n = ws_enc_write_head(data, &ws->enc, flags, payload_len,", "notes": ["C3: ws_enc_write_head writes new frame header after flush"]}, {"n": 1370, "text": "                          &ws->sendbuf, &result);", "notes": []}, {"n": 1371, "text": "    if(n < 0)", "notes": []}, {"n": 1372, "text": "      goto out;", "notes": []}, {"n": 1373, "text": "  }", "notes": []}, {"n": 1374, "text": "", "notes": []}, {"n": 1375, "text": "  /* While there is either sendbuf to flush OR more payload to encode... */", "notes": []}, {"n": 1376, "text": "  while(!Curl_bufq_is_empty(&ws->sendbuf) || (buflen > ws->sendbuf_payload)) {", "notes": ["C1: while loop condition: while(!Curl_bufq_is_empty(&ws->sendbuf) || (buflen > ws->sendbuf_payload))", "C2: while loop at line 1376", "C4: Infinite while loop with no progress when ws->sendbuf_payload==0 and buflen>0"]}, {"n": 1377, "text": "    /* Try to add more payload to sendbuf */", "notes": []}, {"n": 1378, "text": "    if(buflen > ws->sendbuf_payload) {", "notes": ["C1: if(buflen > ws->sendbuf_payload) block calls ws_enc_write_payload which may not increase ws->sendbuf_payload if it returns 0/CURLE_AGAIN"]}, {"n": 1379, "text": "      size_t prev_len = Curl_bufq_len(&ws->sendbuf);", "notes": []}, {"n": 1380, "text": "      n = ws_enc_write_payload(&ws->enc, data,", "notes": []}, {"n": 1381, "text": "                               buffer + ws->sendbuf_payload,", "notes": []}, {"n": 1382, "text": "                               buflen - ws->sendbuf_payload,", "notes": []}, {"n": 1383, "text": "                               &ws->sendbuf, &result);", "notes": []}, {"n": 1384, "text": "      if(n < 0 && (result != CURLE_AGAIN))", "notes": []}, {"n": 1385, "text": "        goto out;", "notes": []}, {"n": 1386, "text": "      ws->sendbuf_payload += Curl_bufq_len(&ws->sendbuf) - prev_len;", "notes": []}, {"n": 1387, "text": "    }", "notes": []}, {"n": 1388, "text": "", "notes": []}, {"n": 1389, "text": "    /* flush, blocking when in callback */", "notes": []}, {"n": 1390, "text": "    result = ws_flush(data, ws, Curl_is_in_callback(data));", "notes": []}, {"n": 1391, "text": "    if(!result) {", "notes": ["C1: if(!result) { *sent += ws->sendbuf_payload; buffer += ws->sendbuf_payload; buflen -= ws->sendbuf_payload; ws->sendbuf_payload = 0; }"]}, {"n": 1392, "text": "      *sent += ws->sendbuf_payload;", "notes": []}, {"n": 1393, "text": "      buffer += ws->sendbuf_payload;", "notes": []}, {"n": 1394, "text": "      buflen -= ws->sendbuf_payload;", "notes": []}, {"n": 1395, "text": "      ws->sendbuf_payload = 0;", "notes": []}, {"n": 1396, "text": "    }", "notes": []}, {"n": 1397, "text": "    else if(result == CURLE_AGAIN) {", "notes": []}, {"n": 1398, "text": "      if(ws->sendbuf_payload > Curl_bufq_len(&ws->sendbuf)) {", "notes